轻轻的我走了，正如我轻轻的来；\n我轻轻的招手，作别西天的云彩。\n那河畔的金柳:
Softly I am leaving, just as softly as I came;
I gently wave my hand, bidding farewell to the western clouds.
The golden willow by the river is a bride in the setting sun;
her shimmering reflection ripples in my heart.
Quietly I am leaving, just as quietly as I came;
I wave my sleeve and take not a single cloud with me.
